  "id": "COMPOUND:17374 - PROTEIN:5407",
  "verbalization": "Mollicellin N appears to have multiple targets that ultimately lead to NCI-H1993 through a series of molecular interactions. The first pathway connects Mollicellin N to A704, which is targeted by palmarumycin CP18, and then to NCI-H1993. The second pathway links Mollicellin N to Leukocyte common antigen, which is targeted by 3Beta-Hydroxyolean-12-En-23,29-Dioic Acid, and then to NCI-H1993. Pathway three provides a similar route, with Mollicellin N targeting A704, which is then targeted by 3Beta-Hydroxyolean-12-En-23,29-Dioic Acid. These pathways suggest that Mollicellin N may act through different molecular mechanisms to influence NCI-H1993, potentially through distinct pathways or targets. The integration of these evidence points indicates that Mollicellin N could be a potential modulator of NCI-H1993, though the exact mechanism of action remains to be fully elucidated.",
